		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2839&amp;p=23264#p23264"><![CDATA[
I had the same black screen after flashing two GD77s with the beta firmware, but I think I figured out the issue!<br><br>On both of them flashing the beta firmware seems to have turned "Safe Power On" to ON. Unfortunately, when you turn on the power there is no indication of what is going on since you get a black screen so it looks like it's bricked.<br><br>To fix it all I had to do was hold SK1 while turning the power on and then go to "Options=&gt;General Options=&gt;Safe Pwr-On" and turn it OFF. After that they both worked fine.<br><br>-David, N9KT<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2972">N9KT</a> — Sun May 07, 2023 7:09 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
